{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\leq 1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Picardfunctor_{X/B} \\to B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pic-functor-curves-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3917f0be3a367c81794b2888a87d299a48b216a0cc9bfefe27f5dc5a6ff499bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5513186b27c211dd9624b38a5850377bc8b236455e7203555288e73542c6786b", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> has relative dimension <MATH_0002> in addition to\nthe other assumptions in this section. Then <MATH_0003>\nis smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4c7567d43ec90e4c13a13238f0fbf1ac47feb64e12bc47e8f758ceda6c3c77a", "unit_id": "tag:0DPK:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to \\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to \\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to \\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Picardfunctor_{X/B} \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pic-curves-smooth}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pic-gerbe-over-pic-functor}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-morphisms-lemma-gerbe-smooth}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-syntomic-smooth-etale-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2bf41b3b3791050b992929b4d77d5f70335c83f2ec43e09ee83c8cc9b9e4c695", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ad31dc884fae4dbf2dd2755377345b6389598658cced63c86806283a68b66469", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> we know that\n<MATH_0001> is smooth. The morphism\n<MATH_0002> is surjective\nand smooth by combining Lemma <REF_0002> with\nMorphisms of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nThus if <MATH_0003> is a scheme and <MATH_0004> is surjective\nand smooth, then <MATH_0005> is surjective and smooth\nand <MATH_0006> is surjective and smooth (because these properties\nare preserved by composition). Thus <MATH_0007>\nis smooth for example by\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b5cb135e1da244869a8ebebd158e16c3aee2288c25427ad274ef51c8cac8be4", "unit_id": "tag:0DPK:proof"}
